  "problem": "What are the dimensions of $ML$, if $M$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix and $L$ is a $3\\times 6$ matrix?",
  "worked_solution": "There are $3$ columns in $M$ and $3$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $M$ equals the number of rows in $L,$ the matrices $M$ and $L$ are conformable for multiplication, and $ML$ is a $4\\times 6$ matrix:\n\n$$\n{M}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{L}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 6}={ML}_{4\\times 6}\n$$",
